(## Explicit adaptations and exclusions) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(- Generic LONGINT/ULONGINT examples use INTEGER and `$i`, the type assigned to) Tj T*
(  group 24. Program and identifier names follow the group's lexical rules.) Tj T*
(- Calls include the mandatory order list of topic 19, even where a generic) Tj T*
(  example omits it. Missing declarative and executable scaffolding is supplied) Tj T*
(  so each illustration becomes an independent complete program.) Tj T*
(- The p.8 generic WHILE examples are adapted to FROM, topic 14. The unknown) Tj T*
(  control rejection example uses an unknown IF inside FROM to exercise the same) Tj T*
(  compile-time modification rule. WHILE syntax is not added to this group.) Tj T*
(- The second valid conversion line on p.4 uses `toul` and describes z as floating,) Tj T*
(  which is inconsistent with this group's `toi` and the same page's mixed-type) Tj T*
(  rule. Its adapted test uses `toi\(x\)+b` with INTEGER b. The original spelling is) Tj T*
(  not silently classified as a valid group-24 input.) Tj T*
(- Topics 11-13, 17, 20-21, 23, 25-28, 30-31, 33 and 35 belong to other groups.) Tj T*
(  Their alternative language features are outside this compiler's assignment.) Tj T*
(  Shared function/copy rules still apply where referenced by the assigned topics.) Tj T*
(- Simple Reduction is excluded because neither member belongs to the 2011 plan.) Tj T*
(- Five numeric incompatibility scenarios remain explicit TP4 boundaries. The) Tj T*
(  suite does not claim that their assembler or eventual runtime behavior has) Tj T*
(  been implemented or validated.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(## Checks and results) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The original verifier runs 107 checks. The course verifier defines 170 scenarios) Tj T*
(and compiles each in both modes, giving 340 additional compiler runs:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(- 103 valid scenarios have their RPN evaluated against explicit observable output.) Tj T*
(- 60 negative scenarios must fail with the required diagnostic and no partial RPN.) Tj T*
(- Seven scenarios are compile-only: five TP4 boundaries and two intentionally) Tj T*
(  nonterminating runtime programs that must not be expanded during compilation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Successful IR also receives structural and metadata checks. Jump destinations) Tj T*
(are local and valid, every CALL has a body, declaration identities are unique in) Tj T*
(effective schemas, formal lists reference parameters, and compile-time reads and) Tj T*
(ARG stores do not survive as runtime operands. MATERIALIZE snapshots must refer) Tj T*
(to declared compile-time fields and numeric constants.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The observable evaluator implements INTEGER division, SINGLEF rounding, lexical) Tj T*
(parents, pending call frames, object receivers and value copies. It does not) Tj T*
(execute the compiler's specialization algorithm to obtain its expected values.) Tj T*
(Output expectations are explicit, or calculated from an independent evaluation) Tj T*
(of source argument order. No production failure was resolved by changing the) Tj T*
(expected source behavior to match the compiler's incorrect output.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The plain-build per-scenario record, including the compiler SHA-256, is in) Tj T*
([tp3_test_results.json]\(tp3_test_results.json\). The instrumented binary's matching) Tj T*
(scenario report is in [tp3_test_results_asan.json]\(tp3_test_results_asan.json\).) Tj T*
(All 340 course runs pass in each report. The original 107 checks also pass on) Tj T*
(both binaries, for 447 compiler checks per build. Both builds have zero Bison) Tj T*
(conflicts and compile with warnings treated as errors.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(## Defects found and corrected) Tj T*
() Tj T*
